# DSEx 02: Evaluate And Optimize

```elixir
repo = if File.exists?("mix.exs"), do: File.cwd!(), else: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)
Mix.install([{:dsex, path: repo}])
```

## Build Train And Dev Sets

```elixir
trainset = [
  DSEx.example(question: "2+2?", answer: "4") |> DSEx.with_inputs(:question),
  DSEx.example(question: "3+3?", answer: "6") |> DSEx.with_inputs(:question)
]

devset = [
  DSEx.example(question: "2 plus 2?", answer: "4") |> DSEx.with_inputs(:question)
]
```

## Define A Metric

```elixir
metric = DSEx.Metrics.exact_match(:answer)
```

## Evaluate A Baseline

```elixir
lm = %{
  module: DSEx.LM.Static,
  opts: [
    handler: fn messages, _opts ->
      prompt = Enum.map_join(messages, "\n", & &1.content)
      if prompt =~ "answer: 4" or prompt =~ "Always answer 4",
        do: %{answer: "4"},
        else: %{answer: "unknown"}
    end
  ]
}

program = DSEx.predict("question -> answer", lm: lm)
evaluator = DSEx.Evaluate.new(devset, metric)
DSEx.Evaluate.run(evaluator, program)
```

## Labeled Few-Shot

```elixir
compiled =
  DSEx.Optimizer.LabeledFewShot.new(k: 1)
  |> DSEx.Optimizer.LabeledFewShot.compile(program, trainset)

DSEx.Evaluate.run(evaluator, compiled)
```

## Random Search

```elixir
compiled =
  metric
  |> DSEx.Optimizer.RandomSearch.new(candidates: 3, demos_per_candidate: 1)
  |> DSEx.Optimizer.RandomSearch.compile(program, trainset, devset)

{
  DSEx.Evaluate.run(evaluator, compiled),
  DSEx.Optimizer.Report.fetch(compiled)
}
```

## Instruction Search

Instruction search changes the program instructions and keeps the candidate
that scores best against the dev set.

```elixir
compiled =
  DSEx.Optimizer.InstructionSearch.compile(
    program,
    metric,
    trainset,
    devset,
    ["Answer unknown.", "Always answer 4."]
  )

DSEx.Optimizer.Report.fetch(compiled)
```

## Optimize Anything

Use artifact optimization when the thing you want to improve is not a DSEx
program yet: a config file, policy text, rubric, template, or other named
artifact.

```elixir
artifact = DSEx.Optimize.Anything.new_artifact(:config, "mode=slow")

report =
  DSEx.Optimize.Anything.optimize(
    artifact,
    fn artifact, _examples ->
      cond do
        artifact.text =~ "mode=fast" and artifact.text =~ "timeout=5" -> 1.0
        artifact.text =~ "mode=fast" -> 0.5
        true -> 0.0
      end
    end,
    trials: 2,
    mutation_fn: fn _artifact, trial, _seed ->
      case trial do
        1 -> "mode=fast"
        2 -> "timeout=5"
      end
    end
  )

report.best
```

## GEPA-Style Reflection

GEPA-style optimization keeps per-example diagnostics, reflects on misses, and
uses Pareto pressure so an improvement for one case does not erase performance
on another.

```elixir
reflection_lm = %{
  module: DSEx.LM.Static,
  opts: [handler: fn _messages, _opts -> %{mutation: "Paris\nconcise"} end]
}

artifact = DSEx.Optimize.Anything.new_artifact(:prompt, "Base")

report =
  DSEx.Optimize.GEPA.optimize(
    artifact,
    fn artifact, examples ->
      %{
        per_example_scores: Enum.map(examples, &if(String.contains?(artifact.text, &1), do: 1.0, else: 0.0)),
        asi: Enum.reject(examples, &String.contains?(artifact.text, &1))
      }
    end,
    examples: ["Paris", "concise"],
    dev_examples: ["Paris"],
    generations: 1,
    reflection_lm: reflection_lm
  )

report.best
```

## Deterministic Advanced Benchmarks

These fixtures are a compact regression check for advanced DSEx behavior. They
belong in production gates rather than application code. Run them through the
release gate when you want evidence that the optimizer and artifact examples
still behave as expected:

```sh
mix production.check
```
